  "description": "The names of a disk's work folder that hold an operation's id, read back. In <workdir>/tmp/: the copy an operation makes, <op-id>.part, and a chunk a repair saves on its way to the trash, <op-id>.<index>.part. In <workdir>/trash/<date>/: an operation's folder, <op-id>, and its folder of chunks, <op-id>.chunks. A name is read only as Atoll writes it: decimal digits 0 to 9, no sign, no leading zero, an id from 1 and an index from 0, each within 63 bits. Any other name names no operation: it is neither removed from tmp/ nor counted when a new catalog starts its operations past those the disks name.",
